IMPORT prelude

-- Fines, Penalties and Infringement Notices Enforcement Act 1994 (Western Australia) -- what happens to a person who does
-- not pay an infringement notice: the final demand, registration with the Fines Enforcement Registry, the order to pay or
-- elect, the notice of intention to enforce, licence suspension, the enforcement warrant and what the Sheriff may not
-- seize, time to pay orders, and the right to elect to have the charge heard by a court instead.
--
-- SEAT: the person given an infringement notice (the Act's "alleged offender", s 11), an individual. Every decision is
-- phrased as that person would ask it: "Can my infringement notice be registered", "Can I still elect to go to court",
-- "Can my licence be suspended", "What must I pay now".
--
-- Provisions covered: s 4A (hardship, as the test for a work and development permit), s 11 (terms), s 12, s 14, s 14A, s 15,
-- s 16(2)(d) and (5), s 17, s 17A, s 18(1), (4), s 19(1), (2A), (3), s 20(1), (2A), s 20A(1)-(3), (5), s 21(1), s 21A(1),
-- s 21B, s 21C(3), s 21H, s 22(4)(b), (5)(a), s 23, s 24, s 26, s 28(1) ("enforceable registered fine", for the WDP
-- contrast), s 46A(e), s 46B, s 46C(2), s 68B(2), s 75, s 101AA(2)-(4), (7).
--
-- Edition: the compilation incorporating amendments up to the Statutes (Repeals and Minor Amendments) Act 2025 s 23
-- (No. 14 of 2025, in operation 26 September 2025), with editorial changes as at 10 October 2024, as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_48845.txt (legislation.wa.gov.au mrdoc_48845, retrieved 7 September 2026).
-- Regulations used: Fines, Penalties and Infringement Notices Enforcement Regulations 1994, version 09-b0-00 in force from
-- 1 July 2026, as deposited at ../../../fines-penalties-and-infringement-notices-enforcement-regulations-1994/registers/
-- source-bundle/mrdoc_49639.txt (retrieved 19 October 2026): r 2B (remote areas), r 8 (property that cannot be seized),
-- r 9 and Schedule 2 Division 1 (Part 3 enforcement fees, as inserted by SL 2026/114), r 10 and Schedule 1 (read only).
--
-- NOT ENCODED: Part 4 (court fines) beyond the work and development permit contrast; Part 5 and Part 7 beyond s 68B and
-- s 75 (seizure and sale procedure, land, vehicle immobilisation and number-plate removal, garnishee orders, the protected
-- earnings and bank amounts of rr 8AA and 8AC, which need a published wage index); the Sheriff's Schedule 2 Division 3
-- fees and r 9(4)-(6) disbursements; s 20(2) and s 21A(5) cancellation "for good reason"; s 20B; s 21D-21G (amending and
-- cancelling a time to pay order); s 22(5)(b)-(e) (refunds after seizure, plate cancellation or garnishee); s 25
-- (continuing offences); s 27 (where the money goes); s 56A-56E (publication of names); s 101 (setting aside a licence
-- suspension order for non-receipt) and s 101B; bodies corporate (s 19(4)). Machinery out: ss 1-2, 5-10B, 13, 105A-109B,
-- Parts 8-9 transitional provisions. The principal enactment's own rules (the modified penalty and its time to pay, the
-- Road Traffic (Administration) Act 2008 instalment scheme and demerit points) are left to that Act and are inputs here.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the
-- individual to whom the law is applied, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Fines, Penalties and Infringement Notices Enforcement Act 1994 -- the questions of the person given an infringement notice`

§§ `s 11, s 12 -- my infringement notice and the facts I can state`

-- s 11: "infringement notice means a notice issued under a written law, other than this Act, to a person alleging the
-- commission of an offence and offering the person an opportunity, by paying an amount of money ... to have the matter
-- dealt with out of court". The "principal enactment" is the law it was issued under. r 3 and Schedule 1 prescribe the
-- enactments Part 3 applies to; Schedule 1 lists the Road Traffic (Administration) Act 2008.
DECLARE `Issuing law` IS ONE OF
    `the Road Traffic (Administration) Act 2008`       -- a road law; listed in Schedule 1
    `another law listed in Schedule 1`                  -- a prescribed enactment, not a road law
    `a law not listed in Schedule 1`                    -- Part 3 does not apply (s 12(1))

-- How far enforcement has gone. Each stage is the latest document issued to me.
--   `the infringement notice`            -- the notice itself, under the principal enactment
--   `a final demand`                     -- s 14 (or s 14A if I missed a road-traffic instalment)
--   `an order to pay or elect`           -- s 17 (or a balance payment order, s 17A): the notice is now registered
--   `a notice of intention to enforce`   -- s 18
--   `a licence suspension order`         -- s 19
--   `an enforcement warrant`             -- s 21A, executed by the Sheriff under Part 7
DECLARE Stage IS ONE OF
    `the infringement notice`
    `a final demand`
    `an order to pay or elect`
    `a notice of intention to enforce`
    `a licence suspension order`
    `an enforcement warrant`

-- r 2B(1): the ASGS Remoteness Structure, July 2016 (ABS 1270.0.55.005).
DECLARE `ASGS remoteness class` IS ONE OF
    `Major Cities of Australia`
    `Inner Regional Australia`
    `Outer Regional Australia`
    `Remote Australia`
    `Very Remote Australia`

DECLARE `My infringement` HAS
    `my age at the time of the offence`                       IS A NUMBER
    `the law it was issued under`                             IS AN `Issuing law`
    `the prosecuting authority is approved by the Registrar`  IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 12(2), s 13(1)
    `I was paying it by road traffic instalments`             IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 14A: paid a first instalment under RTAA Part 5
    `the stage reached`                                       IS A Stage
    `days since the latest document was issued`               IS A NUMBER   -- whole days after the date of issue
    `the time to pay the notice or my next instalment has run out` IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 14(1)(d), s 14A(1)(d)
    `the modified penalty still unpaid`                       IS A NUMBER   -- dollars; s 3 "modified penalty", s 14A(4)(b) "outstanding balance"
    `I have paid it all`                                      IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 3: "paid means paid in full"
    `I have paid part of it`                                  IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 21(1)(b), (7): any part, even by a dishonoured payment
    `I have elected to go to court`                           IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 11 "election", s 14(4)(b), s 21
    `the notice or the proceedings have been withdrawn`       IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 14(1)(b), s 22
    `the time limit for prosecuting has passed`               IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 16(5)
    `a time to pay order has been made`                       IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 21C; s 21H while it is in force
    `my address ASGS class`                                   IS AN `ASGS remoteness class`
    `my postcode is shared with a regional or remote area`    IS A BOOLEAN  -- r 2B(2)(b)
    `my address is in the metropolitan region`                IS A BOOLEAN  -- r 2B(3)(a)
    `my postcode is shared with the metropolitan region`      IS A BOOLEAN  -- r 2B(3)(b)

-- s 12: "(1) This Part does not apply to an infringement notice unless the principal enactment is prescribed ... (2) ...
-- unless the prosecuting authority ... has been approved under section 13(1). (3) This Part does not apply to an
-- infringement notice issued to an alleged offender who, at the time of the alleged offence, was under 17 years old."
@export Does Part 3 of the Fines, Penalties and Infringement Notices Enforcement Act 1994 apply to my infringement notice (s 12)?
GIVEN `my notice` IS A `My infringement` @desc The facts about your infringement notice
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does Part 3 apply to my infringement notice` IF
        (NOT (`my notice`'s `the law it was issued under` EQUALS `a law not listed in Schedule 1`))
    AND `my notice`'s `the prosecuting authority is approved by the Registrar`
    AND `my notice`'s `my age at the time of the offence` AT LEAST 17

-- Not a finished state: the matter is over if I paid in full or the notice or proceedings were withdrawn.
GIVEN `my notice` IS A `My infringement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the matter is still live` IF
        (NOT `my notice`'s `I have paid it all`)
    AND (NOT `my notice`'s `the notice or the proceedings have been withdrawn`)

§§ `s 14, s 14A -- the final demand`

-- s 14(1): applies if "(b) the infringement notice has not been withdrawn; and (c) the modified penalty has not been paid
-- ... and (d) the time for paying the modified penalty has elapsed"; (1A) "the prosecuting authority may issue a final
-- demand". (4): it must say that "unless within 28 days after the date of issue of the final demand -- (a) the modified
-- penalty, and enforcement fees ... are paid ...; or (b) an election is made by the alleged offender ... the infringement
-- notice may be registered". s 14A: the same where I paid a first road-traffic instalment and missed a later one, but the
-- final demand must "(d) state that the alleged offender cannot ... make an election".
@export Can a final demand be issued to me for my unpaid infringement notice (s 14, s 14A)?
GIVEN `my notice` IS A `My infringement` @desc The facts about your infringement notice
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can a final demand be issued to me` IF
        `Does Part 3 apply to my infringement notice` `my notice`
    AND `the matter is still live` `my notice`
    AND `my notice`'s `the stage reached` EQUALS `the infringement notice`
    AND `my notice`'s `the time to pay the notice or my next instalment has run out`

@export How many days does each step under Part 3 give me to act before the next step can be taken?
GIVEN `the stage` IS A Stage @desc The latest document you have been given
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many days the step gives me` IS
    CONSIDER `the stage`
    -- s 14(4), s 14A(4)(c): 28 days after the date of issue of the final demand.
    WHEN `a final demand` THEN 28
    -- s 17(3), s 17A(4): 28 days after the date of issue of the order.
    WHEN `an order to pay or elect` THEN 28
    -- s 18(4): "The due date must not be earlier than 28 days after the date of issue" -- the least I can be given.
    WHEN `a notice of intention to enforce` THEN 28
    -- s 68B(2)(b), s 101AA(3): 14 days after the Sheriff's notice to apply to the Magistrates Court to cancel the warrant.
    WHEN `an enforcement warrant` THEN 14
    -- The infringement notice's own period is set by the principal enactment; a licence suspension order runs until it is
    -- cancelled (s 19(9)(b)). This Act sets no period for either: 0.
    OTHERWISE 0

§§ `s 15, s 16, s 17, s 17A -- registration with the Fines Enforcement Registry`

-- s 15: the prosecuting authority "may register the infringement notice -- (a) if -- (i) a final demand ... is issued
-- under section 14; and (ii) 28 days have elapsed since the date of issue of the final demand; and (iii) the modified
-- penalty, and enforcement fees ... have not been paid ...; and (iv) an election has not been made"; (b) the same for a
-- s 14A final demand, without (iv). s 16(2)(d)(iv)-(v) and (5): the certificate must state that no other proceedings have
-- begun and none have been withdrawn, and "must not be lodged after" the time limit for prosecuting has expired.
-- "28 days have elapsed" is read as 28 or more whole days after the date of issue.
@export Can my infringement notice be registered with the Fines Enforcement Registry (s 15, s 16)?
GIVEN `my notice` IS A `My infringement` @desc The facts about your infringement notice
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my infringement notice be registered` IF
        `Does Part 3 apply to my infringement notice` `my notice`
    AND `the matter is still live` `my notice`
    AND `my notice`'s `the stage reached` EQUALS `a final demand`
    AND `my notice`'s `days since the latest document was issued` AT LEAST 28
    AND (NOT `my notice`'s `I have elected to go to court`)
    AND (NOT `my notice`'s `the time limit for prosecuting has passed`)

§§ `r 9, Schedule 2 Division 1 -- the enforcement fees added to what I owe`

-- r 9(1): the Schedule 2 Division 1 fees "are prescribed as enforcement fees for the purposes of Part 3 of the Act and are
-- to be imposed on an alleged offender at the time indicated". Item 1: final demand $28.30, "imposed when the final demand
-- is issued". Item 2: enforcement certificate $24.10 and item 3: registration $90.50, both "imposed when the infringement
-- notice is registered". Item 4: notice of intention to enforce $59.50, "imposed when a licence suspension order is made or
-- when an enforcement warrant is issued, but not twice". Item 5: enforcement warrant $282.00.
-- r 10 exempts listed prosecuting authorities (the Commissioner of Police among them) "from payment of the fee for
-- registering"; r 9(1) still imposes the fee on the alleged offender, so it is charged here whoever issued the notice.
`final demand fee`            MEANS 28.30
`enforcement certificate fee` MEANS 24.10
`registration fee`            MEANS 90.50
`intention to enforce fee`    MEANS 59.50
`enforcement warrant fee`     MEANS 282.00

@export What enforcement fees have been added to my infringement by the stage it has reached, in dollars (Schedule 2 Division 1)?
GIVEN `the stage` IS A Stage @desc The latest document you have been given
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What enforcement fees have been added` IS
    CONSIDER `the stage`
    WHEN `the infringement notice`           THEN 0
    WHEN `a final demand`                    THEN `final demand fee`
    WHEN `an order to pay or elect`          THEN `fees on registration`
    WHEN `a notice of intention to enforce`  THEN `fees on registration`
    WHEN `a licence suspension order`        THEN `fees on registration` PLUS `intention to enforce fee`
    WHEN `an enforcement warrant`            THEN `fees on registration` PLUS `intention to enforce fee` PLUS `enforcement warrant fee`
    WHERE
        `fees on registration` MEANS `final demand fee` PLUS `enforcement certificate fee` PLUS `registration fee`

-- s 11 "unpaid infringement amount": the modified penalty or its outstanding balance, and enforcement fees, not yet paid
-- or recovered. s 16(6): once registered, payment is accepted only by or on behalf of the Registrar.
@export How much must I pay now to settle my infringement, in dollars (s 11, s 14(4), s 17(3), Schedule 2)?
GIVEN `my notice` IS A `My infringement` @desc The facts about your infringement notice
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What must I pay now` IS
    IF `the matter is still live` `my notice`
    THEN `my notice`'s `the modified penalty still unpaid` PLUS `What enforcement fees have been added` (`my notice`'s `the stage reached`)
    ELSE 0

§§ `s 14(4)(b), s 21 -- my right to elect to have the charge heard by a court`

-- s 21(1): "at any time that is -- (a) after an infringement notice in relation to which a final demand is issued under
-- section 14 is registered ...; and (b) before the modified penalty and enforcement fees, or any part of them, is paid; and
-- (c) before a time to pay order is made ...; and (d) before an enforcement warrant is issued ... the alleged offender ...
-- may make an election." Before registration the final demand itself offers the election (s 14(4)(b)). A s 14A final
-- demand says I "cannot ... make an election" (s 14A(4)(d)), and s 21(1)(a) is confined to s 14 final demands.
@export Can I still elect to have the charge heard and decided by a court instead of paying (s 14(4)(b), s 21)?
GIVEN `my notice` IS A `My infringement` @desc The facts about your infringement notice
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I elect to go to court` IF
        `Does Part 3 apply to my infringement notice` `my notice`
    AND `the matter is still live` `my notice`
    AND (NOT `my notice`'s `I was paying it by road traffic instalments`)
    AND (NOT `my notice`'s `I have elected to go to court`)
    AND (NOT `my notice`'s `I have paid part of it`)
    AND (NOT `my notice`'s `a time to pay order has been made`)
    AND `the stage allows an election` (`my notice`'s `the stage reached`)

GIVEN `the stage` IS A Stage
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the stage allows an election` IF
    CONSIDER `the stage`
    WHEN `a final demand`                   THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an order to pay or elect`         THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a notice of intention to enforce` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a licence suspension order`       THEN TRUE
    -- s 21(1)(d); s 18(5)(da): once a warrant issues "the alleged offender will cease to be entitled to make an election".
    WHEN `an enforcement warrant`           THEN FALSE
    -- Before a final demand the election, if any, is the principal enactment's, not this Act's.
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 23: an order to pay or elect "does not constitute a conviction ... except as provided in sections 25 and 26". s 26(2):
-- where the notice was served under the Road Traffic (Administration) Act 2008 and an order to pay or elect is made, the
-- person "is taken to be convicted of the alleged offence ... for the purposes of the Road Traffic (Authorisation to Drive)
-- Act 2008 section 16(1)(a)". (s 25, continuing offences, is not encoded.)
@export Am I taken to be convicted of the offence for the purposes of the Road Traffic (Authorisation to Drive) Act 2008 s 16(1)(a) (s 23, s 26)?
GIVEN `my notice` IS A `My infringement` @desc The facts about your infringement notice
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I taken to be convicted for driver licensing` IF
        `Does Part 3 apply to my infringement notice` `my notice`
    AND `my notice`'s `the law it was issued under` EQUALS `the Road Traffic (Administration) Act 2008`
    AND (NOT `my notice`'s `I was paying it by road traffic instalments`)
    AND `an order to pay or elect has been made` (`my notice`'s `the stage reached`)

GIVEN `the stage` IS A Stage
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an order to pay or elect has been made` IF
    CONSIDER `the stage`
    WHEN `the infringement notice` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a final demand`          THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `s 18, s 19, r 2B -- the notice of intention to enforce, and licence suspension`

-- r 2B(2): an area is remote if "(a) the area is classified as "Very Remote Australia", "Remote Australia", "Outer
-- Regional Australia" or "Inner Regional Australia" under the ASGS; or (b) the area shares the same postcode as an area
-- referred to in paragraph (a)". (3): not "(a) an area of the State that is located within the metropolitan region; (b) an
-- area of the State that shares the same postcode as an area referred to in paragraph (a)".
@export Is my address in a remote area for the Fines, Penalties and Infringement Notices Enforcement Act 1994 (s 4B, r 2B)?
GIVEN `my notice` IS A `My infringement` @desc The facts about your infringement notice and your address
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my address in a remote area` IF
        (    (NOT (`my notice`'s `my address ASGS class` EQUALS `Major Cities of Australia`))
          OR `my notice`'s `my postcode is shared with a regional or remote area`)
    AND (NOT `my notice`'s `my address is in the metropolitan region`)
    AND (NOT `my notice`'s `my postcode is shared with the metropolitan region`)

-- s 18(1)(a): a notice of intention to enforce may issue if "an order to pay or elect is issued ...; and (ii) 28 days have
-- elapsed since the date of issue ...; and (iii) the unpaid infringement amount ... has not been paid ...; and (iv) an
-- election under section 21 has not been made"; (b) the same for a balance payment order, without (iv). s 21H(2)(a): not
-- while a time to pay order is in force.
@export Can a notice of intention to enforce be issued to me (s 18, s 21H)?
GIVEN `my notice` IS A `My infringement` @desc The facts about your infringement notice
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can a notice of intention to enforce be issued to me` IF
        `Does Part 3 apply to my infringement notice` `my notice`
    AND `the matter is still live` `my notice`
    AND `my notice`'s `the stage reached` EQUALS `an order to pay or elect`
    AND `my notice`'s `days since the latest document was issued` AT LEAST 28
    AND (NOT `my notice`'s `I have elected to go to court`)
    AND (NOT `my notice`'s `a time to pay order has been made`)

-- s 19(1): the Registrar "may make a licence suspension order" once a notice of intention to enforce is issued, "(ii) the
-- due date specified in the notice of intention to enforce has passed; and (iii) the unpaid infringement amount ... has
-- not been paid ...; and (iv) the alleged offender has not made an election". (2A): "cannot ... if -- (a) the alleged
-- offender's last known address is in a remote area; or (b) the alleged offender has given the Registrar information ...
-- that gives the Registrar reasonable grounds to believe that section 20A(3) would apply". s 21H(2)(b): not while a time to
-- pay order is in force. (3): it may disqualify me from holding or obtaining a driver's licence, or a vehicle licence.
-- The due date is read as passed when the days since the notice exceed the 28 the notice must at least give (s 18(4)).
@export Can my driver's licence (or vehicle licence) be suspended for not paying my infringement (s 19, s 21H)?
GIVEN `my notice` IS A `My infringement` @desc The facts about your infringement notice
      `the Registrar has reasonable grounds to believe s 20A(3) would apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have given the Registrar information about your circumstances (urgent medical treatment, your principal means of earning income, or serious hindrance of family or personal responsibilities) that gives reasonable grounds to believe the s 20A(3) grounds would apply
      `the due date in the notice has passed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the due date stated in the notice of intention to enforce has passed
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my licence be suspended` IF
        `Does Part 3 apply to my infringement notice` `my notice`
    AND `the matter is still live` `my notice`
    AND `my notice`'s `the stage reached` EQUALS `a notice of intention to enforce`
    AND `the due date in the notice has passed`
    AND (NOT `my notice`'s `I have elected to go to court`)
    AND (NOT `my notice`'s `a time to pay order has been made`)
    AND (NOT `Is my address in a remote area` `my notice`)
    AND (NOT `the Registrar has reasonable grounds to believe s 20A(3) would apply`)

§§ `s 20, s 20A, s 21H(1), s 22(4)(b) -- getting a licence suspension order cancelled`

-- s 20A(1): an individual "may ... request the Registrar to cancel a licence suspension order"; (2) not "if an election has
-- been made"; (3) if "(a) the licence suspension order deprives the alleged offender of -- (i) the means of obtaining urgent
-- medical treatment for an illness, disease or disability known to be suffered by the alleged offender or a member of the
-- alleged offender's family; or (ii) the principal means of obtaining income with which to pay the unpaid infringement
-- amount; or (b) the licence suspension order seriously hinders the alleged offender in performing family or personal
-- responsibilities."
@export Can I ask the Registrar to cancel the licence suspension order made against me (s 20A(1)-(3))?
GIVEN `my notice` IS A `My infringement` @desc The facts about your infringement notice
      `it deprives me of urgent medical treatment for me or my family` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the suspension takes away your means of getting urgent medical treatment for an illness, disease or disability that you or a family member is known to have
      `it deprives me of my principal means of earning income to pay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the suspension takes away your principal means of earning the income to pay what you owe
      `it seriously hinders my family or personal responsibilities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the suspension seriously hinders you in performing family or personal responsibilities
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I ask the Registrar to cancel my licence suspension` IF
        `my notice`'s `the stage reached` EQUALS `a licence suspension order`
    AND (NOT `my notice`'s `I have elected to go to court`)
    AND (    `it deprives me of urgent medical treatment for me or my family`
          OR `it deprives me of my principal means of earning income to pay`
          OR `it seriously hinders my family or personal responsibilities`)

-- The ways a licence suspension order MUST end:
-- s 20(1): "(a) the relevant modified penalty ... and the associated enforcement fees are paid ... or (b) the alleged
-- offender makes an election" -- it is "taken as having been cancelled"; (2A) "must cancel ... if the alleged offender
-- gives the Registrar a notice stating that the alleged offender's current address is in a remote area"; s 20A(5) if "the
-- Registrar is satisfied that subsection (3) applies" he "must cancel"; s 21H(1) on making a time to pay order "must, as
-- soon as practicable, cancel"; s 22(4)(b) on withdrawal it "is to be taken as having been cancelled".
@export Must the licence suspension order made against me be cancelled (s 20(1), (2A), s 20A(5), s 21H(1), s 22(4)(b))?
GIVEN `my notice` IS A `My infringement` @desc The facts about your infringement notice
      `I gave notice that my current address is in a remote area` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have given the Registrar the approved-form notice that your current address is in a remote area
      `the Registrar is satisfied s 20A(3) applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Registrar is satisfied, on your request, that one of the s 20A(3) grounds applies to you
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my licence suspension be cancelled` IF
        `my notice`'s `the stage reached` EQUALS `a licence suspension order`
    AND (    `my notice`'s `I have paid it all`
          OR `my notice`'s `I have elected to go to court`
          OR `my notice`'s `the notice or the proceedings have been withdrawn`
          OR `my notice`'s `a time to pay order has been made`
          OR `I gave notice that my current address is in a remote area`
          OR `the Registrar is satisfied s 20A(3) applies to me`)

§§ `s 21B, s 21C -- time to pay orders`

-- s 21B(1): I "may apply to the Registrar for a time to pay order in respect of an infringement notice that has been
-- registered"; (3)(a) "at any time after the infringement notice is registered, whether or not a licence suspension order is
-- in force", but (b) not "if -- (i) an enforcement warrant is in force ...; or (ii) the alleged offender has made an
-- election". r 6(2): "The application may be made orally or in writing."
@export Can I apply to the Registrar for a time to pay order (s 21B)?
GIVEN `my notice` IS A `My infringement` @desc The facts about your infringement notice
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I apply for a time to pay order` IF
        `the matter is still live` `my notice`
    AND `my notice is registered` (`my notice`'s `the stage reached`)
    AND (NOT (`my notice`'s `the stage reached` EQUALS `an enforcement warrant`))
    AND (NOT `my notice`'s `I have elected to go to court`)

GIVEN `the stage` IS A Stage
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `my notice is registered` IF `an order to pay or elect has been made` `the stage`

-- s 21C(3): "The Registrar must make a time to pay order ... if the Registrar is satisfied that -- (a) the alleged offender
-- does not have the means to pay the unpaid infringement amount ... within 28 days after the application is made; and (b)
-- the alleged offender's offer to pay ... by a specified date or by regular instalments is reasonable; and (c) either -- (i)
-- the alleged offender has not previously contravened a time to pay order under this Act ...; or (ii) there is a reasonable
-- excuse for any previous contravention". Otherwise (2) he "may" make one "if the Registrar thinks fit". The Registrar's
-- satisfaction is asked, not guessed. s 27A: his decision "is final".
@export Must the Registrar give me a time to pay order on my application (s 21C(3))?
GIVEN `my notice` IS A `My infringement` @desc The facts about your infringement notice
      `the Registrar is satisfied I cannot pay within 28 days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Registrar is satisfied you do not have the means to pay the whole unpaid amount within 28 days after you apply
      `the Registrar is satisfied my offer is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Registrar is satisfied your offer to pay by a set date or by regular instalments is reasonable
      `I have broken a time to pay order before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have previously contravened a time to pay order under this Act (for any infringement or fine)
      `the Registrar is satisfied I had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you have broken one before: whether the Registrar is satisfied there was a reasonable excuse
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Registrar give me a time to pay order` IF
        `Can I apply for a time to pay order` `my notice`
    AND `the Registrar is satisfied I cannot pay within 28 days`
    AND `the Registrar is satisfied my offer is reasonable`
    AND (    (NOT `I have broken a time to pay order before`)
          OR `the Registrar is satisfied I had a reasonable excuse`)

§§ `s 21A, s 68B, s 101AA -- the enforcement warrant`

-- s 21A(1): the Registrar "may issue an enforcement warrant" on the same conditions as a licence suspension order (s 19(1)),
-- and (1A) "whether or not a licence suspension order ... is in force". s 21H(2)(c): not while a time to pay order is in
-- force. Unlike s 19(2A), there is NO remote-area or personal-circumstances bar on a warrant.
@export Can an enforcement warrant be issued against me (s 21A, s 21H)?
GIVEN `my notice` IS A `My infringement` @desc The facts about your infringement notice
      `the due date in the notice has passed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the due date stated in the notice of intention to enforce has passed
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can an enforcement warrant be issued against me` IF
        `Does Part 3 apply to my infringement notice` `my notice`
    AND `the matter is still live` `my notice`
    AND (    `my notice`'s `the stage reached` EQUALS `a notice of intention to enforce`
          OR `my notice`'s `the stage reached` EQUALS `a licence suspension order`)
    AND `the due date in the notice has passed`
    AND (NOT `my notice`'s `I have elected to go to court`)
    AND (NOT `my notice`'s `a time to pay order has been made`)

-- s 101AA(2): I "may apply to the Magistrates Court for an order cancelling the warrant"; (3) "no later than 14 days after
-- the Sheriff gives the applicant the notice under section 68B"; (4) not if I applied before about this or another warrant
-- for the same notice "and the application was refused". (7): the Court may cancel it if I satisfy it that I "received none
-- of the following -- (a) the infringement notice ...; (b) the final demand ...; (c) the order to pay or elect or balance
-- payment order ...; (d) the notice of intention to enforce ...; (e) if a licence suspension order is made ... the notice
-- referred to in section 19(6)(a)". The Court's satisfaction is the fact "I received none of them", as I would state it.
@export Can the Magistrates Court cancel the enforcement warrant issued against me (s 68B, s 101AA)?
GIVEN `days since the Sheriff's s 68B notice` IS A NUMBER @desc Whole days since the Sheriff gave you the notice of your right to apply to cancel the warrant
      `I applied before and was refused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you already applied to cancel this or another warrant for the same infringement notice and were refused
      `I received none of the notices` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you received none of: the infringement notice, the final demand, the order to pay or elect (or balance payment order), the notice of intention to enforce, and any notice confirming licence suspension
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Magistrates Court cancel my warrant` IF
        `days since the Sheriff's s 68B notice` AT MOST 14
    AND (NOT `I applied before and was refused`)
    AND `I received none of the notices`

§§ `s 75, r 8 -- what the Sheriff cannot seize under the warrant`

-- s 75: "The following personal property of a debtor must not be seized or sold under a warrant -- (a) property that the
-- debtor holds in trust for another person ...; (b) wearing apparel and personal items that are of a kind and value
-- prescribed ...; (c) household property that is of a kind and value prescribed ...; (d) property that is used by the
-- debtor to earn income by personal exertion of a value that does not exceed the amount prescribed". r 8(1): apparel of the
-- debtor "to the value of $1 250", of a dependant $1 250, "family diaries, photographs and portraits", "medical and dental
-- aids and equipment"; (2) kitchen and dining $1 250, the debtor's bedroom furniture and bedding $500, a dependant's $200,
-- laundry $200, family entertainment electrical goods $300, a dependant's educational equipment $3 000; (3) "ordinary
-- tools of trade, plant and equipment, professional instruments and reference books to the value of $2 500".
DECLARE `Property kind` IS ONE OF
    `property I hold on trust for someone else`
    `my clothing`
    `a dependant's clothing`
    `family diaries, photographs and portraits`
    `medical and dental aids`
    `kitchen and dining furniture and implements`
    `my bedroom furniture and bedding`
    `a dependant's bedroom furniture and bedding`
    `laundry equipment`
    `family entertainment electrical goods`
    `a dependant's educational equipment`
    `my tools of trade`
    `anything else`      -- for example a car, a boat, jewellery

-- The value up to which property of that kind is protected; -1 for kinds protected whatever their value, 0 for none.
-- Reading: an item of a capped kind is protected while its value is within the cap ("of a ... value prescribed", and for
-- tools "of a value that does not exceed").
@export Up to what value is property of this kind protected from seizure under a warrant, in dollars (s 75, r 8)? -1 means protected whatever its value.
GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Property kind` @desc What the property is
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the protected value` IS
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `property I hold on trust for someone else`     THEN -1
    WHEN `my clothing`                                   THEN 1250
    WHEN `a dependant's clothing`                        THEN 1250
    WHEN `family diaries, photographs and portraits`     THEN -1
    WHEN `medical and dental aids`                       THEN -1
    WHEN `kitchen and dining furniture and implements`   THEN 1250
    WHEN `my bedroom furniture and bedding`              THEN 500
    WHEN `a dependant's bedroom furniture and bedding`   THEN 200
    WHEN `laundry equipment`                             THEN 200
    WHEN `family entertainment electrical goods`         THEN 300
    WHEN `a dependant's educational equipment`           THEN 3000
    WHEN `my tools of trade`                             THEN 2500
    WHEN `anything else`                                 THEN 0

@export Can the Sheriff seize this property of mine under an enforcement warrant (s 75, r 8)?
GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Property kind` @desc What the property is
      `its value` IS A NUMBER @desc Its value in dollars
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Sheriff seize it` IF
        (NOT (`the protected value` `the kind` EQUALS -1))
    AND `its value` GREATER THAN `the protected value` `the kind`

§§ `s 22, s 24 -- withdrawal, and what paying means`

-- s 22(5): "If proceedings are withdrawn ... (a) the alleged offender is to be refunded any amount paid under this Part".
@export How much must be refunded to me if the prosecuting authority withdraws (s 22(5)(a)), in dollars?
GIVEN `the proceedings were withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the prosecuting authority has withdrawn the Part 3 proceedings by a notice of withdrawal
      `what I paid under Part 3` IS A NUMBER @desc How much you paid under Part 3 for this offence, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much must be refunded to me` IS
    IF `the proceedings were withdrawn` THEN `what I paid under Part 3` ELSE 0

-- s 24(1): once the modified penalty and fees "are paid under this Part" and proceedings are not withdrawn, "no
-- proceedings can be commenced and no penalty can be imposed that could not be commenced or imposed if the alleged offender
-- had been convicted"; (2) payment "is not to be regarded as an admission" unless the principal enactment says so.
@export If I pay in full under Part 3, am I protected from any further prosecution or penalty that a conviction would bar (s 24(1))?
GIVEN `my notice` IS A `My infringement` @desc The facts about your infringement notice
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I protected from further prosecution` IF
        `my notice`'s `I have paid it all`
    AND (NOT `my notice`'s `the notice or the proceedings have been withdrawn`)

§§ `s 28, s 46A-46C, s 4A -- why a work and development permit is not for an infringement`

-- s 46A: a WDP lets "an offender ... discharge the offender's liability to pay the amount owed in respect of a fine" by
-- unpaid work, treatment, a course, or "(e) if the offender has not reached 25 years of age when the permit is issued -- a
-- mentoring programme". s 28(1) (Part 4): "fine means a monetary penalty imposed on an offender by a court"; s 46C(1) an
-- approved sponsor applies "in relation to the offender and an enforceable registered fine", and (2) only after "a notice of
-- intention to enforce has been issued under section 42". Part 3 offers no WDP: an unpaid infringement notice is enforced
-- by licence suspension and warrant. Only if I elect, am convicted and fined does the debt become a Part 4 fine.
-- s 46B(1): "An offender is eligible for a WDP if the offender is experiencing hardship"; s 4A(1): financial hardship,
-- family violence, mental illness, disability, homelessness, or alcohol or other drug use problems, and (2) not limited to
-- those; s 46B(2) financial hardship counts only "to an extent that affects the offender's capacity to pay a fine". The
-- Registrar relies on the sponsor's assessment (s 46C(4)) and "may issue" the permit (s 46D(1)).
DECLARE `What I owe` IS ONE OF
    `an unpaid infringement notice under Part 3`
    `a court fine registered under Part 4`

@export Can an approved sponsor apply for a work and development permit for what I owe (s 46B, s 46C)?
GIVEN `the debt` IS A `What I owe` @desc Whether you owe an unpaid infringement notice or a fine a court imposed
      `I am experiencing hardship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are experiencing hardship (s 4A): financial hardship that affects your capacity to pay, family violence, mental illness, disability, homelessness, alcohol or drug problems, or another kind
      `a Part 4 notice of intention to enforce has been issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a court fine: whether a notice of intention to enforce has been issued under s 42
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can a sponsor apply for a work and development permit for me` IF
        `the debt` EQUALS `a court fine registered under Part 4`
    AND `I am experiencing hardship`
    AND `a Part 4 notice of intention to enforce has been issued`

@export Can a work and development permit for my court fine include a mentoring programme (s 46A(e))?
GIVEN `my age when the permit is issued` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in years when the permit would be issued
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my permit include mentoring` IF `my age when the permit is issued` LESS THAN 25
